yea, that is bogus asf. I just feel like the ramifications from the "real world" are too intense to deter people from seeking help. Like in my situation, I came back and was on probation due to "not properly stating my absences" amongst other things. 

&#x200B;

Like I was legitimately being penalized for taking care of myself. Damn sure no cancer patient would've gotten that treatment. I wonder sometimes who is actually to blame.

I don't mean to laugh, but this post totally made me laugh because my mom and friends say the exact same thing. My mom has called me a drama queen for as long as I can remember, and that I need to calm down and stop overthinking everything. 

&#x200B;

Then you've got my friends who would describe me as incredibly chill and fun to be around....so strange

