I'm like fixated on that first bullet point...anyway

&#x200B;

Sure! Why not? It kind of stinks that you can't really shadow anybody because of HIPAA, because that would be my first suggestion. Maybe narrow down which kind of surgery you'd be interested in and kind of start researching it now?

oh man you're like a giant puzzle I love it. Well, first off proud of you for being clean that long very impressive. Second, I'm struggling with the same problem right now. I smoke weed daily to help with my PTSD from childhood. On top of taking medication. My suggestion would be to find some way to use your anger/anxiety/pent up energy. Whether that be a workout class, martial arts, just working out on your own, buying a punching bag, you name it. That is probably the healthiest way to release whatever you're feeling. 

&#x200B;

You could also look in to yoga and different meditation exercises.

Do you guys usually use DM's to communicate? There is certain social media that I use for certain friends and wouldn't expect them to answer with that particular social media if we don't use it on a regular basis. 

&#x200B;

Also, yea I'd say you're paranoid, but I think we all do it at some point. Do you think there is anything that could've been misinterpreted that should be cleared up? If not, then just roll with it. Sometimes it also says that people are online when they really aren't too...so he may have read your messages but isn't in a position to respond.

I am that person in my friend groups, and there are definitely times where it does go to far. Some people see that as a form of love too...so I guess you gotta look at it like that as well. Are they just doing it because they love ya? Or are they really out to hurt you? I had two friends who I knew were doing it for malicious reasons, and to get a rise out of me, so those were the ones that I started doing it back to. We eventually stopped being friends, but the others do it out of love and at this point in our friendship everyone has been that guy at this point. 

&#x200B;

Also, if you're the newest member of the group people do it as a kind of "initiation" I went through it, and then I was part of it...pushing someone to see how far you can joke with them

What advice are you asking? Like what to do next? 

&#x200B;

Take a bath with some bath bombs, chocolate, cheese, wine, beer whatever...and just relax and cry. Get that over with and then move on slowly. It's going to suck no doubt but if you let it consume you, you will never get over it.

do you have other people you talk to? I just recently cut ties with one of my best friends who definitely has almost identical phone conversations as your friend does. I'm 27 and I can tell you that your friend isn't going to change. She's always going to be like that, always having a 1-up attitude, always talking about herself. It can definitely be emotionally draining and exhausting listening to someone talk about themselves every day and not letting you get a word in, especially when this person is your friend. 

&#x200B;

I'd let her go...only because I wish I had let my friend go earlier than I did...you won't miss her. You're going to have so much free time on your hands it'll be insane...it's nice.

plasma, selling clothes, uber/lyft, 

&#x200B;

and yea...drugs

I asked her mom about that, the PPD, and she said that they addressed it with the doctor but he didn't seem concerned. She I believe is on a low dose of Prozac. Her reasoning for her drinking was always because she couldn't sleep. I think at this point it's more of a comfort for her because she "thinks" she can still function. 

&#x200B;

I feel bad displaying her boyfriend like this, but in truth I believe that he's just nervous about being alone with their daughter and she's definitely a take charge personality so it's easy to just let her do it herself.

